        <IRI>http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma67498</IRI>
        <Literal>Anatomical structure, each instance of which has a maximal complement of instances of  two or more types of tissue or one or more types of essential morphologic unit, a predominantly bona fide boundary and intrinsic vasculature and neural network. Examples: liver, lung, kidney, stomach, urinary bladder, gall bladder.</Literal>
