    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma82353</IRI>
        <Literal>Cunningham 72:342 - Each levator costae is a small triangular muscle arising from the transverse processes of a vertebra from the 7th cervical to the 11th thoracic inclusive.  It fans out as it descends to be inserted into the external surface of the rib below, between the tubercle and the angle.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
